<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
  <meta name="description" content="A small personal desktop utility project.">
  <title>Local Message Monitor</title>
  <style>
    :root { color-scheme: light; --ink:#202433; --muted:#5e6678; --accent:#6258d9; --surface:#fff; --bg:#f4f5fb; }
    * { box-sizing: border-box; }
    body { margin:0; font-family: system-ui, -apple-system, Segoe UI, sans-serif; background:var(--bg); color:var(--ink); line-height:1.6; }
    header { padding:22px max(24px, calc((100% - 960px)/2)); background:#fff; border-bottom:1px solid #e5e7ef; }
    .brand { font-weight:750; letter-spacing:.2px; }
    main { max-width:960px; margin:0 auto; padding:72px 24px; }
    .eyebrow { color:var(--accent); text-transform:uppercase; font-size:.8rem; font-weight:750; letter-spacing:.12em; }
    h1 { max-width:720px; font-size:clamp(2.3rem, 6vw, 4.3rem); line-height:1.08; letter-spacing:-.04em; margin:14px 0 20px; }
    .intro { max-width:680px; color:var(--muted); font-size:1.15rem; }
    .card { margin-top:36px; background:var(--surface); padding:26px; border:1px solid #e5e7ef; border-radius:18px; box-shadow:0 12px 35px #1e24400b; }
    h2 { margin-top:0; }
    footer { max-width:960px; margin:0 auto; padding:0 24px 36px; color:var(--muted); font-size:.9rem; }
    a { color:var(--accent); }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
  <header><div class="brand">Local Message Monitor</div></header>
  <main>
    <div class="eyebrow">Personal desktop project</div>
    <h1>A small utility for organizing message-based workflows.</h1>
    <p class="intro">Local Message Monitor is a personal software project focused on helping a user review relevant messages and prepare information for manual confirmation.</p>
    <section class="card">
      <h2>About this project</h2>
      <p>This page describes a personal desktop utility. It is not affiliated with Telegram, Thrill, or any other third-party service.</p>
      <p>Any actions on third-party websites remain subject to the relevant service's rules and the user's confirmation.</p>
    </section>
  </main>
  <footer>Personal project page · No account sign-in or personal information is collected by this static page.</footer>
</body>
</html>
